---
import { capitalize } from "@utils/utils";
import client from "@data/client.json"
---
<h1>Excellent {capitalize(client.industry.service)} Solutions in {client.address.city}, {client.address.stateFull}</h1>
    <p>
      Welcome to the ultimate hub for all your {client.industry.service} needs! As an elite
      {client.industry.sector} {client.industry.service} company in {client.address.city}, {client.address.state}, we are devoted
      to offering flawless painting services. Our evolution into one of the
      foremost {client.industry.industry} service providers is due to our team of highly
      competent and well-versed {client.industry.profession} who are eager to rejuvenate your space.
      Our goal is to ensure that every interaction with us leaves a lasting
      impression.
    </p>
    <h2>Selecting the Right Choice with {client.name}</h2>
    <p>
      When it comes to {client.industry.service}, it's vital to take into account the
      established colors of your home, such as brick, stonework, and roofing.
      The ideal color schemes are those that complement these existing features.
    </p>
    <p>
      Consider embracing a shade that enhances the color of an unpainted section
      - like highlighting the brown in your brick or a shade of green from your
      stonework.
    </p>
    <p>
      It's also essential to remember that your home is part of a community; its
      aesthetic is influenced by neighboring homes and the surrounding
      landscape. While you may not want your house to be the exact color as your
      neighbor's, selecting a shade that harmonizes with nearby homes can be
      beneficial.
    </p>
    <p>
      Additionally, be mindful that certain colors are more suited to specific
      environments. For instance, earth tones are typically a great choice for
      natural, wooded areas.
    </p>
    <h2>Quality {capitalize(client.industry.service)} Options with {client.name}</h2>
    <p>
      The external factors such as extreme temperatures, humidity, and
      continuous sun exposure can deteriorate the exterior paint of our homes.
      When paint breaks down, it can expose cracks which allow damaging moisture
      to enter the home. Quality paint can protect against severe weather while
      allowing damaging moisture to escape.
    </p>
    <p>Nowadays, there are numerous options for weather-resistant paints.</p>
    <p>
      Elastomeric coatings are gaining popularity; these coatings maintain their
      elasticity across a broad temperature range, making them ideal for homes
      in areas with extreme weather conditions.
    </p>
    <h2>{client.name}’s {capitalize(client.industry.service)} Process</h2>
    <h3>Surface Preparation</h3>
    <p>
      Proper surface preparation is fundamental to any painting project. Various
      methods can be employed, and it's crucial to determine what preparation is
      needed to achieve the desired results. Some preparation techniques are
      designed for long-lasting results, while others are aimed at enhancing the
      appearance.
    </p>
    <h3>Washing</h3>
    <p>
      The first step in ensuring a high-quality finish is a clean surface. If
      there is any mold, we will hand wash the area with an appropriate cleaning
      solution. Pressure washing the exterior removes mold, dirt, and old paint,
      providing a solid base for the new paint to adhere to.
    </p>
    <p>
      Pressure washing can also be used to clean exterior driveways, sidewalks,
      and stone walls by removing grease, dirt, and moss. As pressure washers
      are powerful machines, only trained professionals will handle this
      equipment.
    </p>
    <h3>Drop Cloths</h3>
    <p>
      {client.name} uses heavy-duty canvas drop cloths. We place them
      around the home where scraping will occur. This practice protects your
      plants, pavement, and soil, and enables easier cleanup at the end of the
      day. The result is a spotless environment once the job is complete.
    </p>
    <h3>Caulking</h3>
    <p>
      Caulking is a pliable sealant used in gaps where expansion and contraction
      are expected, such as around windows and doors. It prevents moisture from
      entering the wood, which is often the cause of paint failure around these
      areas.
    </p>
    <p>
      Only paintable latex caulking is used on your home. Silicone caulking is
      not paintable and must be removed and replaced before painting as it is
      typically used for bathrooms.
    </p>